These terms cover use of `www.eaglespancorp.com`, the website of Eagle Span
Corporation. Using the site means accepting them. They govern the website only:
the work we do on a vehicle is governed by the estimate, the work order and the
invoice for that job, not by this page.

## The content here

The text, images, layout and code on this site belong to Eagle Span Corporation
or are used with permission. You are welcome to read it, print it, and quote it
with attribution. Republishing it as your own, or reproducing the site
wholesale, is not permitted.

## What the content is for

The maintenance intervals, diagnostic values and repair guidance published here
are general information written by our technicians. They are not a substitute
for a manufacturer’s specification or for a technician looking at your vehicle.
Where a manufacturer’s figure and something on this page disagree, follow the
manufacturer.

Prices, availability and the scope of any service can change without notice.
Nothing on this site is a binding quote — a quote comes from the shop, for a
specific vehicle and a specific job.

## Using the site

Do not attempt to break, overload or gain unauthorized access to this site or
the systems behind it, and do not use automated tools to scrape or copy it
wholesale. Do not use the site or anything on it for an unlawful purpose.

## Availability

We keep the site running and accurate, but we do not promise it will be
available without interruption or free of errors, and we are not liable for loss
arising from its temporary unavailability or from a mistake in its content.

## Links to other sites

Links to sites we do not run are provided for convenience. We do not control
them and are not responsible for what is on them.

## Governing law

These terms are governed by the laws of the State of North Carolina, United
States.

## Changes

We may revise these terms. The current version is always the one on this page,
